Kills of peacefuls aren't a problem, as long as the kill is
immediately followed up by the killing of a hostile.  Given the
large number of hostiles in the dungeon, even without paying
attention, it's rare to have a problem, except in special cases:
if the gnomes and dwarfs are peaceful in the mines (especially
since your max alignment typically isn't very high when you get
there), or gremlins on a waterly level, if you don't get them
before they start to replicate.  And possibly a few other cases
as well, but those are the two I've encountered.

